>> title: Batata Harra, Air Fryer
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: potato, lebanese, air fryer, basket, cilantro, chiles
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> dish: batata-harra
>> kit: Air Fryer
>> aka: air fryer batata harra, spicy potatoes in the air fryer, basket batata harra, Lebanese spicy potatoes
>> servings: 4
>> time: 35 min
>> slack: forgiving — a cube that is pale goes back for three minutes, and the garlic and cilantro go on off the heat where nothing can burn
>> washing-up: the basket, the bowl
>> capacity: 4 — one 5.7 L air fryer basket, roast, air fry
>> keeps: not at all — the cubes slump and their crust turns back to skin; it is a ten-minute dish to make again

>> step: Written for a preheated 5.7 L basket. From cold, add three minutes. A 3.5 L basket is two batches, not more minutes.
No parboil and no pan of oil. The cubes go in raw and come back to the bowl.

>> step: cut in cubes, dry hard, toss with oil in the bowl
Cut @russet potatoes{1 1/4%lb}(570 g; peeled, in 3/4-in cubes), dry them hard in a towel and toss in a #bowl{} with @olive oil{1 1/2%Tbs}, @kosher salt{1%tsp}.

>> step: roast in the basket 200°C (400°F), 16–20 min, one layer
Roast @&(~1)oiled cubes{} in a preheated #air fryer basket{} at 200°C (400°F) for ~air fry{18%min}, one layer.

>> step: toss the basket at ten minutes — a corner cracks, it does not dent
Toss @&(~1)potatoes{} by shaking the basket once.

>> step: toss hot in the same bowl, off the heat
Toss @&(~1)crisp cubes{} with @garlic{4%cloves}(grated), @cilantro{1/2%cup}(chopped), @red chile flakes{1%tsp}, @lemon{1/2}(juiced).

>> step: The plain file is a pan of frying oil plus two bowls. This is the basket and the bowl the potatoes came out of.
Five things down to two, and the toss is the same toss.
